<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Tuesday 105,000 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Tuesday 105,000 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tuesday's estimated interior Iowa and southern Minnesota hog marketings were 105,000 head, compared with 113,000 a week ago and 108,000 a year ago. Estimates included generally about 60 percent Carcass Base Hogs. Barrows and gilts sold $1.00 per cwt higher than midsession Monday. Trade slow to moderate for good demand and light to moderate offerings.</p>
<p>				    Country		  Plants</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	     53.00 -54.00	   54.00 -55.00</p>
<p>few			 52.50		    53.50</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>260-280 lbs	     51.00 -54.00	   51.50 -55.00</p>
<p>US 2-4   43-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>280-300 lbs	     47.50 -52.50	   48.00 -53.50</p>
<p>Sows:   generally steady to $2.00 higher, advance 500 lbs. up</p>
<p>US 1-3  300-450 lbs.  44.00 -46.00	   44.00 -46.00</p>
<p>450-500 lbs.	    47.00 -49.00	   48.00 -49.00</p>
<p>500 lbs. up	     52.00 -56.00	   52.00 -57.00</p>
<p>Note: Prices quoted represent sales of hogs averaging 73-74 pct carcass Yields with mostly 1.00-1.25 inches of last rib backfat and 47-48 pct. lean.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk, 312-983-7347--</p>
